      "content": "The most abundant elements by mass in the body of a healthy human adult are: Oxygen (61.4%); Carbon\n(22.9%), Hydrogen (10.0%); and Nitrogen (2.6%). The weight which a 75 kg person would gain if all\n<sup>1</sup>H atoms are replaced by <sup>2</sup>H atoms is: ",
